                <pb facs="0903" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.032/46</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-31T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 31, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1872. The Mexican Congress has now finally approved the use by the Executive of
                    his exercise of special powers in finance with the exception of the paper decree
                    and has granted him special powers to raise or lower import and export duties as
                    in his option conditions may warrant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
